## FOOTNOTE CITATION FORMAT (ACADEMIC STYLE)

**CRITICAL**: All footnotes MUST follow academic citation format:

```
Author. (Year, Month Day). Title. Publication, URL
```

### Examples:

**News article:**
```
[^1]: EU-Startups. (2022, April). Berlin-based Staex raises €1.65 million for its unique and sustainable Web3 stack for IoT. eu-startups.com, https://www.eu-startups.com/2022/04/berlin-based-staex-raises-e1-65-million-for-its-unique-and-sustainable-web3-stack-for-iot/
```

**Company source:**
```
[^2]: Staex. (2024). NEXA: World's first Web3-operated drone corridor. staex.io, https://www.staex.io/nexa
```

**Interview source:**
```
[^3]: Mikityuk, A. (2025, December). Interview with Staex CEO by Maze2 SA CEO. Headquarters confirmed as Potsdam, Germany.
```

**Editorial/Analysis:**
```
[^4]: Editorial analysis. (2025, December). Strategic positioning based on Deutsche Telekom heritage.
```

### Format Rules:
1. **Author**: Organization name OR "Last, First Initial." for individuals
2. **Date**: (Year, Month Day) or (Year, Month) or (Year) or (Year, Quarter)
3. **Title**: Article/page title in sentence case
4. **Publication**: Domain without www or https
5. **URL**: Full URL at end, no square brackets

### DO NOT USE this old format:
```
❌ [^1]: [Source Name](URL) - Description
```

### ALWAYS USE academic format:
```
✅ [^1]: Author. (Year, Month Day). Title. publication.com, https://full-url.com
```

---

## SOURCING GUIDELINES

### Priority Order for Sources
1. **External third-party sources** (news, research, partner announcements) - HIGHEST PRIORITY
2. **Staex official announcements** with specific page URLs (staex.io/blog/specific-post)
3. **CEO/founder interviews** (cite: "Interview with Staex CEO by [interviewer], [date]")
4. **Official website** with specific page (staex.io/nexa, staex.io/mint) - use sparingly

### AVOID
- Generic "Staex Official" links pointing only to homepage (staex.io)
- Footnotes without any URL (just descriptions/analysis)
- Over-reliance on company's own claims without external validation

### When Using Company Sources
- Always indicate it's a company source: "[Staex Blog](url) - Company source"
- Prefer external validation when available
- Cross-reference major claims with third-party coverage

